<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  THE CHIP. A LABEL, never a control.
  22-components.md 10, 32-master-plan-android.md 8.4.
  ============================================================================

  Android ships no chip component at all today: five TextViews wearing shape
  drawables do the job, one of them with 2dp vertical padding, and the protocol chip
  measures 4.0:1. This is the replacement.

  A chip is NEVER clickable. A clickable pill is a Tertiary button or a Segment —
  that is the whole boundary between this component and those, and the style already
  nails it shut (clickable false, checkable false, ensureMinTouchTargetSize false:
  expanding a label to 48dp would push every row apart for nothing).

  IT NEVER SHRINKS AND NEVER ELLIPSISES ITS OWN LABEL (5.6). It measures
  wrap_content and the text beside it yields. singleLine is here to keep a chip one
  line tall, not to truncate it.

  COLOUR IS NEVER THE ONLY SIGNAL (6.3): every status chip carries the WORD. A bare
  coloured dot next to a label that already states the state is decoration and gets
  deleted. There is no fourth status hue (R12) — «Отменён» is neutral, because a
  cancelled payment is not a warning.

  THE CLASS IS A STYLE, AND A STYLE BINDS AT INFLATION. This file is the Neutral
  class — protocol, transport, «Отменён», «Это устройство». A chip whose class is
  known at build time declares its own class directly at the call site:
      style="@style/Widget.Departament.Chip"             neutral, Russian label
      style="@style/Widget.Departament.Chip.Technical"   Latin token or figure
      style="@style/Widget.Departament.Chip.Accent"      THE tariff badge, and nothing else
      style="@style/Widget.Departament.Chip.Status.Ok"   «Оплачено», «Активна»
      style="@style/Widget.Departament.Chip.Status.Warn" «В обработке», «Истекает»
      style="@style/Widget.Departament.Chip.Status.Error" «Ошибка», «Истекла»
  A chip whose class CHANGES at runtime (a subscription's health) needs a binder that
  maps state to class — see the note filed with the ui/component owner. Do not hand
  -paint a fill or a text colour onto this view; that is how the four-hue drift
  started.
-->
<com.google.android.material.chip.Chip
    xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:id="@+id/chip"
    style="@style/Widget.Departament.Chip"
    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
    android:singleLine="true"
    tools:text="Активна" />
